From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Swanson <rswanson05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:00:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: report when an agent's state began and let clients move
 panes

Agents carry a state_since_ms token with the wall-clock time of their
last state change, so clients can show how long an agent has been
working or waiting. A live handoff carries each agent's state and start
time, and keeps the start when detection re-finds the same state.
pane.move joins the client shell methods so the sidebar can move panes
between spaces. Client snapshots give each agent a git_branch token
with the branch checked out where it works, read at most every few
seconds per folder.

